&Q000509 = A hymn to Ḫaia for Rīm-Sîn (Rīm-Sîn B)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.2.6.9.2
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.2.6.9.2&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div uru A

A.1. en ŋeštug₂ mah šu du₇ sa₂ gal-e pad₃-da
#lem: en[lord]; ŋeštug[ear]; mah[great]; šu[hand]; du[perfect]; sa[advice]; gal[big]; pad[find]
#tr.en: Lord, perfect in august wisdom and recognised for his mighty counsel, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.1

A.2. {d}ha-ia₃ dub gal-gal ha-ha-za ŋeštug₂-ŋeštug₂-ga peš-peš
#lem: Haia[1]DN; dub[tablet]; gal[big]; haza[hold]; ŋeštug[ear]; peš[thick]
#tr.en: @wDN{Ḫaia}, who holds the great tablets, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.2

A.3. šid-du₃ hal-an-kug igi zag til galam-ma-ke₄ e₂-GEŠTUG₂-{d}NISABA-ke₄
#lem: šid[count]; Halankug[1]TN; igi[eye]; zag[side]; til[make complete]; galam[skilful]; E₂.GEŠTUG₂.NISABA.k[1]TN
#tr.en: who enriches the deep wisdom! Accountant of Ḫal-an-kug, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.3

A.4. pisaŋ-dub-ba e₂-gal an ki-a kiŋ₂ kilib-ba šid-šid
#lem: bisaŋdubak[archivist]; egal[palace]; an[sky]; ki[place]; kiŋ[work]; kilib[total]; šid[count]
#tr.en: having the final overview of the arts of @wDN{Nisaba's} house of wisdom; palace archivist of heaven and earth, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.4

A.5. gi kug-ga šu ŋal₂-le im nam-tar gal-gal mul-mul
#lem: gi[reed]; kug[pure]; šu[hand]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; im[clay]; namtar[fate]; gal[big]; mul[shine]
#tr.en: who keeps count of every single assignment, who holds a holy reed-stylus and covers the great tablets of destiny with writing! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.5

A.6. gal-an-zu inim ŋeštug₂ degₓ(RI)-ge ud-bi-še₃ an kug-ga-ra
#lem: galanzu[wise]; inim[word]; ŋeštug[ear]; deg[gather up]; ud[sun]; An[1]DN; kug[pure]
#tr.en: Wise one, who prompts holy @wDN{An} with words and attention at the appropriate times; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.6

A.7. kišib-ŋal₂ a-a {d}en-lil₂-la₂-ke₄ lu₂ tam-ma e₃ erim₃ e₂-kur-ra
#lem: kišibŋal[seal bearer]; aya[father]; Enlil[1]DN; lu[person]; tam[clean]; e[leave]; erim[storeroom]; Ekur[1]TN
#tr.en: seal-holder of Father @wDN{Enlil}! He who brings forth the holy objects from the treasure-house of @wTN{E-kur}; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.7

A.8. he₂-du₇ eš₃-e abzu-a siki bar-ra la₂-la₂ en {d}nu-dim₂-mud-ra
#lem: hedu[ornament]; eš[shrine]; Eʾabzu[1]; siki[hair]; bar[outside]; la[hang]; en[lord]; Nudimmud[1]DN
#tr.en: ornament of the @fsux{abzu} shrine, wearing his hair loose for Lord @wDN{Nudimmud}! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.8

A.9. {d}ha-ia₃ šag₄-gada-la₂ e₂-u₆-nir-ra uz-ga kug lu-lu
#lem: Haia[1]DN; šaggadala[priest]; Eunir[1]TN; uzga[priest]; kug[purify]; lu[abundant]
#tr.en: @wDN{Ḫaia}, linen-clad priest of @wTN{E-unir}, who stocks the holy @fsux{uzga} precinct; learned scholar of the shrine @wTN{E-kiš-nu-ŋal}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.9

A.10. umun₂ ak-ak eš₃ e₂-kiš-nu-ŋal₂-la₂-ke₄ mu mah-bi gal-la
#lem: umun[knowledge]; ak[do]; eš[shrine]; Ekišnuŋal[1]TN; mu[name]; mah[great]; gal[big]
#tr.en: whose august name is great, whose mind is discerning; who dwells in the great dining-hall alongside the maiden @wDN{Ningal}! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.10

A.11. šag₄ inim-ŋal₂ ki-sikil {d}nin-gal-e unu₇ gal-e til₃-la
#lem: šag[heart]; inimŋal[eloquent]; kisikil[young woman]; Ningal[1]DN; unu[dwelling]; gal[big]; til[live (of a single person)]
#tr.en: Fair of features, beloved spouse of @wDN{Nun-bar-še-gunu} and augustly renowned father-in-law of Father @wDN{Enlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.11

A.12. muš₃-me sag₉ nitalam₂ ki aŋ₂ {d}nun-bar-še-gu-nu
#lem: mušme[face]; sag[goodness]; ŋidlam[(equal ranking) spouse]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; Nunbaršegunu[1]DN
#tr.en: the Great Mountain; junior administrator, possessor of wisdom, acknowledged in heaven and earth, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.12

A.13. lu₂ mu mah mussa kur gal a-a {d}en-lil₂-la₂-kam
#lem: lu[person]; mu[name]; mah[great]; mussa[son-in-law]; kur[mountain(s)]; gal[big]; aya[father]; Enlil[1]DN
#tr.en: who receives the tribute for the gods, the abundance of mountains and seas! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.13

A.14. saŋŋa ban₃-da igi-ŋal₂-tuku pad₃-da an ki-bi-da-ke₄
#lem: saŋŋa[an official]; banda[junior]; igiŋaltuku[wise]; pad[find]; an[sky]; ki[place]
#tr.en: Interpreter of the obscurity of @wDN{Enlil's} (?) words, skilful one who steers the august princely divine powers, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.14

A.15. gu₂-un diŋir-re-[e-ne] šu gid₂-i ma-dam kur ab su₃-ud-da inim-ma-ni bur₂-e
#lem: gun[load]; diŋir[deity]; šu[hand]; gid[long]; madam[abundance]; kur[mountain(s)]; ab[sea]; sud[distant]; inim[word]; bur[spread out]
#tr.en: with …… girt at his side! Formed (?) with a broad heart, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.15

A.16. gal-zu me mah nam-nun-na#-ka u₅ tur₃ zag keše₂-da
#lem: galanzu[wise]; me[Being]; mah[great]; namnun[magnificence]; u[ride]; tur[animal stall]; zag[side]; kešed[bind]
#tr.en: holding in his hands the holy divine plans of the temple of @wSN{Eridug}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.16

A.17. šag₄ daŋal sur-ra ŋiš-hur kug-ga e₂ eridug{ki}-ga-ke₄ šu dab-be₂
#lem: šag[heart]; daŋal[wide]; sur[press]; ŋešhur[plan]; kug[pure]; e[house]; Eridug[1]SN; šu[hand]; dab[seize]
#tr.en: @wDN{Ḫaia}, who wears the ceremonial robe during pure lustrations of the @fsux{engur}! @wDN{Indagara}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.17

A.18. {d}ha-ia₃ lu₂ šu-luh sikil-la engur-ra-ke₄ tug₂-ba₁₃ tug₂ la₂-la₂
#lem: Haia[1]DN; lu[person]; šuluh[ritual cleansing]; sikil[pure]; engur[(cosmic) underground waters]; ba[garment]; tug[textile]; la[hang]
#tr.en: administrator who performs the opening of the mouth for the gods in the heavens and in the underworld, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.18

A.19. {d}indagara saŋŋa₇(|GA.BALAG|) utah-he₂ kur-ta ka du₈-u₃ diŋir-re-e-ne-ke₄
#lem: Indagara[1]DN; saŋŋa[an official]; utah[heaven]; kur[mountain(s)]; kag[mouth]; du[spread]; diŋir[deity]
#tr.en: and who is versed in the meaning of obscure tablets; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.19

A.20. šag₄ dub-ba su₃-ud-da zu-a galam ak-ak diŋir gal-gal-e-ne
#lem: šag[heart]; dub[tablet]; sud[distant]; zu[know]; galam[skilful]; ak[do]; diŋir[deity]; gal[big]
#tr.en: craftsman of the great gods! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.20

A.21. šu-nir-nir {ŋiš}gag-a du₃-du₃ saŋ sig₉-ga ki galam hur kalam-ma
#lem: šunir[emblem]; gag[nail]; du[build]; saŋ[head]; sig[put into]; ki[place]; galam[skilful]; hur[scratch]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]
#tr.en: He who fixes the standards on their pegs, planner (?) who artfully excavates (?) the soil of the Land, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.21

A.22. ki šu tag-tag unu₇ sig₇-ga an-šar₂ kur gal-ra
#lem: ki[place]; šu[hand]; tag[touch]; unu[dwelling]; sissig[green-yellow]; Anšar[1]DN; kur[mountain(s)]; gal[big]
#tr.en: who decorates the floor and makes the dining-hall attractive for @wDN{Anšar} and the Great Mountain! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.22

A.23. saŋ il₂ mah eš₃-e abzu-ta dug₄-ga-ni še-ga
#lem: saŋ[head]; il[raise]; mah[great]; eš[shrine]; Eʾabzu[1]; dug[speak]; šeg[agree]
#tr.en: Tall and with head high, he whose utterances from the @fsux{abzu} shrine are favourable, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.23

A.24. lu₂ saŋ keše₂ ninda babbar sikil-la šu dab-be₂ e₂ diŋir-re-e-ne
#lem: lu[person]; saŋ[head]; kešed[bind]; ninda[bread]; babbar[white]; sikil[pure]; šu[hand]; dab[seize]; e[house]; diŋir[deity]
#tr.en: who carefully holds the pure white loaves of the house of the gods! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.24

A.25. {d}ku₃-su₃ {d}indagara e-ne-ne-da nu an nu-sikil-la ki nu-dadag-ge
#lem: Kusug[1]DN; Indagara[1]DN; anene[they]; nu[not]; an[sky]; sikil[pure]; ki[place]; dadag[bright]
#tr.en: @wDN{Kusu} and @wDN{Indagara}, without whom heaven would not be pure nor earth bright, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.25

A.26. u₂ gal-gal sud-sud an {d}en-lil₂-la₂ unu₇ mah-ne-ne-ke₄
#lem: u[plant(s)]; gal[big]; sud[distant]; An[1]DN; Enlil[1]DN; unu[dwelling]; mah[great]
#tr.en: continual providers of the great meals of @wDN{An} and @wDN{Enlil} in their grand dining-hall! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.26

A.27. lu₂ muš₃ kug-ga igi du₈ en {d}nu-dim₂-mud-e
#lem: lu[person]; muš[flat space]; kug[pure]; igi[eye]; du[spread]; en[lord]; Nudimmud[1]DN
#tr.en: He who gazes upon the holy precinct, upon Lord @wDN{Nudimmud}; he who holds the holy bronze vessels, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.27

A.28. zabar kug-ga šu ŋal₂-le šag₄ hul₂-hul₂ bar sig₁₀-sig₁₀-ge₅
#lem: zabar[bronze]; kug[pure]; šu[hand]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; šag[heart]; hul[rejoice]; bar[outside]; sig[put into]
#tr.en: who makes hearts rejoice and soothes spirits! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.28

A.29. lugal-ŋu₁₀ nam-mah-zu šir₃-ra ga-am₃-i-i
#lem: lugal[king]; nammah[greatness]; šir[song]; e[bring out]
#tr.en: My king, I shall praise your eminence in song! @wDN{Ḫaia}, I will declare your greatness perpetually! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.29

A.30. {d}ha-ia₃ nam-gal-zu gi₁₆-sa-še₃ ga-am₃-pad₃-pad₃-de₃-en
#lem: Haia[1]DN; namgal[greatness]; gilsa[treasure]; pad[find]
#tr.en: Who among the gods is fitted like you for the holy divine powers? 
#etcsl: line-id=A.30

A.31. a-ba za-a-gin₇ diŋir-re-e-ne-ke₄ me kug-ga-aš tum₂-ma
#lem: aba[who?]; zaʾe[you]; diŋir[deity]; me[Being]; kug[pure]; tum[suitable]
#tr.en: Your beloved spouse is the maiden @wDN{Nisaba}, the great queen of queens. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.31

A.32. nitalam ki aŋ₂-zu ki-sikil {d}nisaba nin gal nin-e-ne
#lem: ŋidlam[(equal ranking) spouse]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; kisikil[young woman]; Nisabak[1]DN; nin[lady]; gal[big]; nin[lady]
#tr.en: @wDN{Ninlil}, who was born of her holy womb, the august wife of @wDN{Nunamnir}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.32

A.33. u₃-tud-da šag₄-ga-ni {d}nin-lil₂-la₂ dam mah {d}nu-nam-nir-ra
#lem: utud[give birth (to)]; šag[heart]; Ninlil[1]DN; dam[spouse]; mah[great]; Nunamnir[1]DN
#tr.en: sits with her on the dais of @wTN{E-kur} with head raised high, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.33

A.34. barag e₂-kur-ra-ke₄ saŋ il₂-la an-še₃ ši-in-da-til₃
#lem: barag[sanctum]; Ekur[1]TN; saŋ[head]; il[raise]; an[sky]; til[live (of a single person)]
#tr.en: uniquely entitled to behave as queen of the gods, the peerless goddess. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.34

A.35. nam-nin diŋir-re-e-ne-ke₄ me-er-ga-bi al-ak-e diŋir zag ša₄ nu-tuku
#lem: namnin[ladyship]; diŋir[deity]; merga[first one]; ak[do]; diŋir[deity]; zag[side]; sa[equal]; tuku[acquire]
#tr.en: In the @fsux{abzu} shrine, @wDN{Enki} has bestowed his incantations of life on you, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.35

A.36. za-e ninda₂ gal ŋalga zid pad₃-da en₃ tar-tar diŋir-re-e-ne-ke₄
#lem: zaʾe[you]; ninda[breeding bull]; gal[big]; ŋalga[(fore)thought]; zid[right]; pad[find]; en[cvne]; tar[cut]; diŋir[deity]
#tr.en: great breed-bull, who are recognised for your right understanding, who constantly care for the gods, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.36

A.37. {d}ha-ia₃ me šum₂-šum₂-mu kiŋ₂ aŋ₂-e ki-šu-peš igi zu-zu-me-en
#lem: Haia[1]DN; me[Being]; šum[give]; kiŋ[work]; aŋ[measure]; kišupeš[cultic place]; igi[eye]; zu[know]
#tr.en: @wDN{Ḫaia}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.37

A.38. {d}en-ki-ke₄ eš₃-e abzu-ta mu₇-mu₇ nam-til₃-la-ni mu-ra-rig₇
#lem: Enkik[1]DN; eš[shrine]; Eʾabzu[1]; mu[incantation]; namtil[life]; rig[donate]
#tr.en: you who operate effectively the assigning of divine powers, who mark out the cult places. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.38

A.39. en ŋi₆-par₃-e mu-ni-ib-huŋ-en saŋ sig₁₀ mu-ni-ib-ŋar-re-en
#lem: en[priest]; ŋipar[cloister]; huŋ[hire]; saŋ[head]; sig[put into]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: You appoint the high priest for the @fsux{ŋipar} and install him there as its caretaker. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.39

A.40. sipad kalam-ma-ra ŋidru mah ud su₃-ra₂ šu-ni-še₃ bi₂-ib-dab₅-e-en
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; ŋidru[scepter]; mah[great]; ud[sun]; sud[distant]; šu[hand]; dab[seize]
#tr.en: You make the shepherd of the Land hold in his hands the august sceptre until distant days. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.40

A.41. {d}ha-ia₃ diŋir kalam-ma a-ra-zu uŋ₃ šar₂-ra ŋiš tuku-me-en
#lem: Haia[1]DN; diŋir[deity]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; arazu[supplication]; uŋ[people]; šar[numerous]V/i; ŋeš[tree]; tuku[acquire]
#tr.en: @wDN{Ḫaia}, you are the god of the Land who gives ear to the prayers of all the people. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.41

A.42. za-e diŋir gal-gal-e-ne uŋ₃ daŋal-la šu-ni-še₃ bi₂-ib-dab₅-e-en
#lem: zaʾe[you]; diŋir[deity]; gal[big]; uŋ[people]; daŋal[wide]; šu[hand]; dab[seize]
#tr.en: You make the king hold the widespread people in his hands for the great gods. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.42

A.43. a-a {d}en-ki abzu-ta ed₂-da-ni-ta
#lem: aya[father]; Enkik[1]DN; abzu[(cosmic) underground water]; e[leave]
#tr.en: When Father @wDN{Enki} comes forth from the @fsux{abzu}, he assigns (?) its greatness to you, @wDN{Ḫaia}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.43

A.44. {d}ha-ia₃ nam-gal-bi za-e ša-mu-re-da-an-aŋ₂
#lem: Haia[1]DN; namgal[greatness]; zaʾe[you]; aŋ[measure]
#tr.en: You cause the people who are in its midst to lift their necks towards heaven; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.44

A.45. uŋ₃ šag₄-ba i₃-ni-me-a-ke₄ gu₂-bi an-še₃ ši-bi₂-ib₂-zi-zi
#lem: uŋ[people]; šag[heart]; e[speak]; gu[neck]; an[sky]; zig[rise]
#tr.en: you make its population pass their days in rejoicing. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.45

A.46. nam-lu₂-ulu₃-bi ud asil-la₂ mi-ni-ib-zal-zal-le-ne
#lem: namlulu[humanity]; ud[sun]; asilala[joy]; zal[pass time]
#tr.en: You keep all its people forever contented. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.46

A.47. uŋ₃ šar₂-ra-bi šag₄ hul₂-la ud ul-le₂-a-aš bi₂-ib-ak-e-en
#lem: uŋ[people]; šar[numerous]V/i; šag[heart]; hul[rejoice]; ud[sun]; ul[distant time]; ak[do]
#tr.en: You establish festivals in the houses of the great gods; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.47

A.48. e₂ diŋir gal-gal-e-ne ezen ab-ŋar-re-en giri₁₇-zal ši-bi₂-du₈-du₈-un
#lem: e[house]; diŋir[deity]; gal[big]; ezem[festival]; ŋar[put]; kirizal[joy]; du[spread]
#tr.en: you spread splendour. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.48

A.49. saŋ-kal saŋ-kal-e diŋir-re-e-ne-ke₄ ŋiš-šub gal-gal uŋ₃ til-la-ni
#lem: saŋkal[foremost]; saŋkal[foremost]; diŋir[deity]; ŋeššub[lot]; gal[big]; uŋ[people]; til[complete]
#tr.en: Leader, leader (?) of the gods, complete the great fates of the people. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.49

A.50. igi sag₉-ga-zu nam-til₃ si-a lugal-ra igi zid bar-mu-un-ši-ib
#lem: igi[eye]; sag[good]; namtil[life]; si[fill]; lugal[king]; igi[eye]; zid[right]; bar[place outside]
#tr.en: Look favourably upon the king with your gracious gaze that is full of life. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.50

A.51. nun {d}ri-im-{d}suen bal hul₂-hul₂ ud su₃-ud-da šu zid ŋar-mu-na-ab
#lem: nun[prince]; Rimsin[1]RN; bala[turn]; hul[rejoice]; ud[sun]; sud[distant]; šu[hand]; zid[right]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: Duly grant a joyous reign of long days to prince @wRN{Rīm-@wDN{Sîn}}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.51

A.52. im nam-til₃-la-ke₄ du-ri₂-še₃ nu-kur₂-ru mu-bi gub-i₃
#lem: im[clay]; namtil[life]; duri[forever]; kur[different]; mu[year]; gub[stand]
#tr.en: marking its years on the tablet of life, forever unalterable. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.52

A.53. sipad {d}ri-im-{d}suen nam-en-bi an {d}en-lil₂-la₂ ki he₂-aŋ₂-e-ne
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; Rimsin[1]RN; namen[the office of en-priest]; An[1]DN; Enlil[1]DN; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]
#tr.en: May @wDN{An} and @wDN{Enlil} love the shepherd @wRN{Rīm-@wDN{Sîn}} in the office of high priest. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.53

A.54. lu₂ šir₃-ra-ke₄ za₃-mi₂-zu ka-bi-a mi-ni-ib-dug₃-ge-ne
#lem: lu[person]; šir[song]; zamin[praise]; kag[mouth]; dug[good]
#tr.en: The singers will make your praise resound sweetly in their mouths; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.54

A.55. {d}ha-ia₃ lu₂ šir₃-ra-ke₄ za₃-mi₂-zu ka-bi-a mi-ni-ib-dug₃-ge-ne
#lem: Haia[1]DN; lu[person]; šir[song]; zamin[praise]; kag[mouth]; dug[good]
#tr.en: @wDN{Ḫaia}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.55

A.56. en an ki lugal abzu-a za₃-mi₂-bi mah-a
#lem: en[lord]; an[sky]; ki[place]; lugal[king]; abzu[(cosmic) underground water]; zamin[praise]; mah[great]
#tr.en: the singers will make your praise resound sweetly in their mouths. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.56

A.57. a-a {d}en-ki lugal abzu-a za₃-mi₂-zu dug₃-ga
#lem: aya[father]; Enkik[1]DN; lugal[king]; abzu[(cosmic) underground water]; zamin[praise]; dug[good]
#tr.en: Lord of heaven and earth, king of the @fsux{abzu}, its praise is august. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.57

@div trailer 

A.58. u₁₈-ru₁₂-bi-im
#lem: uru[literary subscript]
#tr.en: Its @fsux{uru}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.58

@end trailer

@end uru

@div ŋišgiŋal B

B.59. {d}ha-ia₃ diŋir kalam-ma ga-til₃-e ki aŋ₂ nun {d}ri-im-{d}suen-e a₂ bad tal₂-ni he₂-me-en
#lem: Haia[1]DN; diŋir[deity]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; gatil[vow]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; nun[prince]; Rimsin[1]RN; a[arm]; bad[open]; tal[broad]; me[be]
#tr.en: @wDN{Ḫaia}, god of the Land, who loves the words @q{“Give me life!”}, extend your broad arms round prince @wRN{Rīm-@wDN{Sîn}}. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.59

@div trailer 

B.60. ŋiš-gi-ŋal₂-bi-im
#lem: ŋešgiŋal[musical refrain]
#tr.en: Its @fsux{ŋišgiŋal}. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.60

@end trailer

@end ŋišgiŋal







